WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.200
Performance means doing the real task under normal conditions.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.720
You troubleshoot the production issue, deliver the presentation, write the report,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.480
lead the meeting, or make the operational decision.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.480
Practice is different.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.920
Practice isolates parts of the task so they can be improved.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.955
It creates room to slow down, repeat, compare,

00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:18.015
and correct without the full pressure of live performance.

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:20.395
People often confuse being busy with getting better.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:22.850
A busy day may include many opportunities to perform,

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.480
but performance pressure can make learning harder.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.185
In production work, people are trying to finish, avoid mistakes, and meet commitments.

00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:32.295
They may not have time to examine the weak part of the skill.

00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:36.075
Practice time lets them step away from pure output and work on the mechanism behind better

00:00:36.075 --> 00:00:36.800
output.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.510
Safe practice environments can include rehearsal, drills, simulations, worked examples,

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.596
targeted exercises, and low-stakes review.

00:00:42.596 --> 00:00:47.675
A developer might practice threat modeling on a small example before doing it on a major

00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:48.400
system.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.010
A manager might rehearse a difficult conversation before the real meeting.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.636
An analyst might compare several decision records to identify where assumptions were weak.

00:00:55.636 --> 00:00:59.135
Separating learning time from production pressure does not mean practice is artificial or

00:00:59.135 --> 00:00:59.800
irrelevant.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.530
Good practice is connected to real work,

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.400
but it is designed for improvement instead of immediate delivery.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.780
The point is to create a space where mistakes are visible, feedback is usable,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.920
and the learner can repeat the critical part before the stakes are higher.
